1. Unusual marker genes in GSE176078 — V(D)J variable region genes dominating several clusters
In the Wilcoxon marker gene analysis for GSE176078, clusters 3–9 show top markers dominated by immunoglobulin and T-cell receptor variable region genes (IGHV, IGLV, TRAV, TRBV families) rather than canonical cell-type markers. Two possible explanations: (1) these clusters genuinely represent plasma cells or cycling lymphocytes where V(D)J recombination products are highly expressed, or (2) these genes were captured in HVG selection and are inflating the marker results without adding biological meaning.
I have re-run the marker analysis filtering out V(D)J prefixes and the cleaned markers look more interpretable — bringing both versions to compare.
Question for supervisor: Should V(D)J genes be excluded from HVG selection entirely for this analysis, or retained and filtered only at the marker interpretation stage? And do the plasma cell / lymphocyte clusters make biological sense given this is a breast tumour microenvironment dataset?
